# PowchainService Construction

## The Supplier Origin

The 4th argument (`finalizedStateSupplier`) is created in the constructor as a lambda that **does derive its data from `BeaconChainService`**. It's wrapped in a `Supplier` intentionally, as the comment explains: `"making it a Supplier ensures that BeaconChainService has been started and RecentChainData has"` been initialized when called.

The supplier lambda:
```java
final Supplier<Optional<BeaconState>> finalizedStateSupplier =
    () -> {
      final RecentChainData recentChainData =
          beaconChainService.getBeaconChainController().getRecentChainData();
      if (recentChainData.isPreGenesis()) {
        return Optional.empty();
      }
      return Optional.of(recentChainData.getStore().getLatestFinalized().getState());
    };
```

So yes — it pulls `RecentChainData` from `beaconChainService.getBeaconChainController()`, checks pre-genesis, and returns the latest finalized state otherwise.

## The PowchainService Build

Inside the `powchainService(...)` helper method:
```java
final PowchainService powchainService =
    new PowchainService(
        serviceConfig,
        tekuConfig.powchain(),
        maybeExecutionWeb3jClientProvider,
        finalizedStateSupplier);
serviceConfig.getEventChannels().subscribe(FinalizedCheckpointChannel.class, powchainService);
return Optional.of(powchainService);
```

## The Full Helper Method

```java
private Optional<PowchainService> powchainService(
    final TekuConfiguration tekuConfig,
    final ServiceConfig serviceConfig,
    final Optional<ExecutionWeb3jClientProvider> maybeExecutionWeb3jClientProvider,
    final Supplier<Optional<BeaconState>> finalizedStateSupplier) {
  if (tekuConfig.beaconChain().interopConfig().isInteropEnabled()
      || (!tekuConfig.powchain().isEnabled() && maybeExecutionWeb3jClientProvider.isEmpty())) {
    return Optional.empty();
  }
  if (!tekuConfig.powchain().isDepositContractLogsSyncingEnabled()) {
    EVENT_LOG.depositContractLogsSyncingDisabled();
    return Optional.empty();
  }
  final PowchainService powchainService =
      new PowchainService(
          serviceConfig,
          tekuConfig.powchain(),
          maybeExecutionWeb3jClientProvider,
          finalizedStateSupplier);
  serviceConfig.getEventChannels().subscribe(FinalizedCheckpointChannel.class, powchainService);
  return Optional.of(powchainService);
}
```

## Summary

The supplier is defined in the constructor and passed down to the helper, which uses it as the 4th constructor argument. The method returns an empty `Optional` early in two cases: when interop is enabled or powchain/execution provider aren't available, and when deposit contract logs syncing is disabled — since, per the comment, `"PowchainService is only used for deposit contract logs syncing"`.

